// ═══ THE NEAR FOREGROUND: tall grass, flowers on stalks (never yellow), fence posts — they whip past and STREAK ═══
//   A level lens a metre or two up cannot see the ground at its feet, so the foreground is TALL (0.4–1.3 m): its tops
//   poke up into the bottom of the frame. Placed per 0.8 m cell of course distance at depths nearDA..nearDB (analytic,
//   stateless). Slower than streakMin px a frame they are drawn; faster, each becomes marker streaks of its colours.
const DH_SD_FLOWERS = ['#ee6aa7', '#ffffff', '#b98ae0', '#8fb7e6', '#e0323f', '#f2a7c4', '#f07a1a'];
