// MM_CLOISTER3 · EP3 scenes 1 and 2: THE HALO CLOISTER FOR ENDANGERED SPECIES (the orphanage), outside and in.
//   📖 "the foreboding black building made of obsidian bricks" (JAVA JOSE) · "its massive domed ceiling supported by an
//   elliptical array of dark vesicular stone pillars" · "the smaller door built into the grand entrance of the
//   institution onto the massive stone stairs" · "its title, engraved in shimmering white at the entrance: Halo Aliquid
//   Nihil" · "a curved horizon warped like a fisheye fun house mirror … the planet's uncanny arcing grid of, repetative,
//   nondescript cul-de-sacs" · "People in Mowersville take their lawns too seriously." · Mook's room: "watching through
//   my porthole" · "this nervous energy that had sewn me to my bed" · "I unpick my bed sutures" (misadv 274-330).
//   🎬 Claude's design from those words (Mook's to keep or change): the black glass-brick front with its dome, two rows
//   of brass portholes (his is lit), the grand arch with the small door in it, wide basalt stairs, mown lawns falling
//   away downhill to Mowersville: rows of pink box houses on a horizon that bends (his 2020 title card's town). Inside,
//   his room: black stone walls, the porthole, a cot along the wall with its blanket stitched down (the sutures), his
//   drawings pinned up, the door to the hall.
