//   mm_town9.js (the 8 kinds) and mm_stadium7.js (the bowl).
//   ✅ 🗣 "grown-ups of many kinds" · the doc: "lots of hedgehogs, geese and sheep, in their own colours" · ✅ call 36.
//   🎬 THE RULES (Mook's to keep or change):
//    · THEY STAND. Half the town is furniture (a clock, a mailbox, a trash can, a lamppost, a popcorn machine) and can't
//      sit down, so the whole town stands on the tiers, one row to a tier, like a terrace at a football match.
//    · SMALL AT THE FRONT, TALL AT THE BACK, like a class photo: the crabs in the front rows, the owls and the clocks on
//      the top tiers, so every face can see the plinth (and the camera can see every face).
//    · FAMILIES: they come in twos to fives of a kind, in their family's own colours (the kind's two colours turned
//      round the colour wheel together). Never red | blue (the last three of Mook's kind), never the Yellow.
//    · AISLES: eight stairways from the floor to the rim (the tunnel is the south one). The WEST aisle is the one Mook
//      runs up to the rim in the final.
//   THE PAINTER: each tier segment's people are ONE item, sorted right after that segment's stone, so the stone round
//    them sorts the way EP7 built it. Standing on the tread (nothing hangs over the edge), the only stone that can be
//    in front of them is their own step's edge, seen from below: each one is cut on that line.
