// mm_koi11.js · EP11 THE BIG ONE · THE KOI (🎬 Claude's design, 2026-10-14, ☐ for Mook's yes before any shot uses it)
//   📄 "It rises: a koi, enormous and old, scarlet and white, scales as big as plates, moss and little lilies growing on its
//   back like a garden. It looks at Bronconius with one huge eye." · Rose: "That's not a fish. That's a neighbourhood."
//   (a shadow "wider than the dock is long": 18 m) · the B-plot's LUCY is a star "cut like a gem"; the koi's eye is the A-plot's
//   rhyme (the match: "the koi's eye, sinking → the gem card's glow").
//   WHAT IT IS: EP8's mesh sculptor (m8Tube, m8Draw: faces lit one by one, inked where the body turns away) made into a fish.
//    · KOHAKU: a white body, scarlet islands across the back (and a red cap on the head), the belly pale; the red only on
//      top, as a real kohaku's is.
//    · SCALES AS BIG AS PLATES: each face of the body is one scale (about 0.6 m), drawn as a plate's rim along its back edge;
//      a few old scales gone pearl.
//    · OLD: a heavy brow over the eye, whiskers (two pairs of barbels) gone long, pale scars, the fins frayed at the edges.
//    · THE GARDEN: moss along the ridge of its back from behind the head to the dorsal fin, small lily pads and pink lilies
//      on the moss, reeds of its own.
//    · THE EYE: big (0.7 m across), a pale gold iris round a deep pupil and a soft highlight; it turns to look (o.look).
//   kk11Koi(g, C, o)  paints it. o: { p: [x, y, z] the middle of its body, yaw (its heading, 0 = +z), pitch (nose up),
//     L (length, 16 m), t (film time: the tail's slow sway, the fins), bend (−1…1, a turn), look: [x, y, z] (the eye's target),
//     light }
//   kk11Foot(o)  its outline on the water's plane (for the water laid over its sunk part)
//   Every global starts kk11 / KK11.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
