// ═══ D5 · THE KOI ═══
//   📄 501.3 "The fish stops. Bronconius stops, nose-down in the water, an arm's length from it." (D4) · 503.7 "It rises: a koi,
//   enormous and old, scarlet and white, scales as big as plates, moss and little lilies growing on its back like a garden." ·
//   509.7 "It looks at Bronconius with one huge eye. Eye to eye." · 514.1 "Slowly, he lets go of the rod. The hook drops out of
//   the koi's lip by itself." · 518.1 "The koi sinks back into the dark, in no hurry at all." · 522.5 Rose and Gil crash out of the
//   reeds (C2) · 524.5 ROSE "Where is it?" · 526.2 BRONCONIUS "…Gone." · 526.9 Leo, asleep, says nothing at all.
//   o.T: s from 📄 501.313 (the sounds: the koi's deep 2.5 · its sinking 17.0).
