// mm_cab12.js · EP12 THE MATCHSTICK HOUSE · INSIDE THE GROOVE MACHINE (🎬 Claude, 2026-10-15). Loads after mm_yard3.js (yd* camera),
//   mm_groove12.js (Otis's pictures), mm_core.js.
//   EP12-SCRIPT: "a tie-dye ceiling, a bead curtain, a lava lamp, a rack of Mondays Man mugs, a tape deck, a steering wheel as big
//   as a bike wheel. Everything leans: the camper is still nose-down in its crater." · "Three levers by the wheel, no words on
//   them, only little drawings: a wheel, an anchor, a sail." · the glovebox (a map, sunflower seeds, the first editions with a
//   black gem in each one's corner, humming) · the READY light on the dash · the seat built for a giant.
//   THE ROOM, in its own metres (x to its right = the door side, y up, z forward to the windshield; the floor at y 0):
//     the living end z −2.7 … 0.85 (the door in the right wall at z −0.2 … 0.6), the bead curtain at z 0.85, the cab z 0.85 … 2.2:
//     the driver's seat on the left (x −0.45), the passenger's bench on the right, the dash at z 1.95, the split windshield.
//   TILT: the whole room is turned by o.tilt (rad, + = nose down, the crater) about its middle; the lens stays level, so
//   everything leans; what hangs (the beads, the lava's blobs, the mugs on their hooks) hangs straight down.
