// ── _geo/episodes/ep14/blocks/mm_gait14.js
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// mm_gait14.js · EP14 · THE FHAT'S WADDLE-SPRINT (🎬 Claude, 2026-10-20, the Revision Pass: "The Fhat on two legs: a new gait.
//   A beanie's waddle-sprint: short stride, high cadence, no slide. Built and turn-checked before the chase exists.")
//   Loads LAST (after mm_chase14.js: it replaces s14FhatRun; the old one is kept there as s14FhatRunV1).
// WHY: the old run (fhatDraw's walk { ph: s / 0.9, stride: 0.45 }) lifted each foot while it swung BACK and kept it down while
//   it swung FORWARD, and its feet swept ~10 cm a step while the body went 45 cm: a planted foot skated ~35 cm every step.
// THE GAIT, exact, from the distance run (not the clock), so it can't slide at any speed:
//   · a step every λ = v / f metres (f steps a second rises with speed, capped at 9.5: each leg's cycle stays ≥ 6 frames at 30 fps);
//   · in each step ONE foot is planted for its first σλ metres, PINNED in the world (its offset from the hips runs +a → −a exactly
//     as the body passes over it; a ≤ 0.55 of its body radius: its legs are 7 cm); then the body FLIES, real gravity (apex g·t²/8),
//     while that foot swings forward on a lifted arc to its next plant, two steps on;
