//   A crank turns a wavy wire; four birds stand on it with their beaks open, each tongue a different sign (an arrow, an
//   exclamation mark, a loop, a hook). Here the wire is a reel mower's axle: turn the crank and they sing and mow.
//   Below, the pit Klee left under his machine; above it a strip of fresh-cut lawn. Pen over a rose and violet wash on a
